===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*bʰrewh₁-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|brawne}}, from {{der|en|fro|braon||slice of meat, fleshy part, buttock}}, from {{der|en|frk|*brādon}}, {{m|gmw-pro|*brādan}}, accusative form of {{m|gmw-pro|*brādō||roasted meat, ham}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*brēdô||meat, roast}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*bʰrē-||to burn, heat}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*bʰrewh₁-||to boil, bubble, burn}}. Akin to {{cog|goh|brāto||tender meat}} ({{cog|de|Braten||roast}}), {{cog|ang|brǣde}}, {{m|ang|brǣd|t=flesh, meat}}, {{cog|non|bráð||raw meat}}.

